# Which bank implementation answers behind the gate — operator-owned, like okgate.yaml.
#
# okgate spawns the bank upstream with the MCP SDK's default environment plus
# only the keys declared in okgate.yaml's `upstreams[].env`, so exporting
# BANK_UPSTREAM_MODE in your shell never reaches the gated upstream. This file is
# the same knob on our side of that boundary: values here are read when the
# process env does not define them, so a shell override still wins for standalone
# runs (`python -m banking_agent.bank.server`).
#
# Nothing here changes what is enforced. Tiers (¥1,000 / ¥5,000), the ¥5,000/day
# cap, MFA, the loop breaker, the kill switch and `unknown: block` all come from
# okgate.yaml and banking_agent/gate/, byte-for-byte identical in both modes.
#
# Uncomment to point the gate's bank upstream at a running Postman
# Banking-API-Demo (`npm run dev:api` in that repo) instead of the mock ledger.
# Prefer 127.0.0.1 over `localhost`: the demo listens on IPv4, and on Windows a
# ::1-first lookup shows up as "Postman Demo API is not running".

# BANK_UPSTREAM_MODE=postman_demo
# POSTMAN_DEMO_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000
# POSTMAN_DEMO_API_PREFIX=/api/v1
# POSTMAN_DEMO_API_KEY=1234
# POSTMAN_DEMO_TRANSFER_PATH=/api/v1/transactions
# POSTMAN_DEMO_CURRENCY=COSMIC_COINS
# POSTMAN_DEMO_TIMEOUT_S=10
# POSTMAN_DEMO_RUN_ID=
#
# The demo has no CNY — its enum is COSMIC_COINS / GALAXY_GOLD / MOON_BUCKS.
# Leave the alias off unless you want a functional (not monetary-accurate) demo
# run: with it off, a CNY transfer is refused with `currency_mismatch` rather
# than silently re-denominated, which would make the ¥ thresholds count a unit
# the bank never charged. `banking_agent/demo/run.py` speaks CNY, so it needs
# this set to 1 to complete against the demo.
# POSTMAN_DEMO_ALLOW_CURRENCY_ALIAS=0
